# Unity 6 (C#)

- Unity 6 API renames: `Rigidbody.velocity` → `linearVelocity`, `drag` → `linearDamping`, `angularDrag` → `angularDamping`. `FindObjectOfType` → `FindFirstObjectByType` / `FindAnyObjectByType`; `FindObjectsOfType` → `FindObjectsByType(FindObjectsSortMode.None)`.
- Use the Input System package (`UnityEngine.InputSystem`, Input Actions) if it's installed. Don't use `Input.GetKey` / `Input.GetAxis` in that case.
- Cache component references in `Awake` (`GetComponent` once). Never call `GetComponent`, `Find` or `Camera.main` every frame in `Update`.
- Physics in `FixedUpdate`; input reading and visuals in `Update`.
- Expose fields with `[SerializeField] private`, not public fields.
- Compare Unity objects with `== null` (or `if (obj)`); don't use `?.` or `??` on `UnityEngine.Object`.
- Use `CompareTag("Enemy")`, not `tag == "Enemy"`.
- Avoid allocations in hot paths (no LINQ, string concatenation or `new` lists per frame). Pool frequently spawned objects.
- Use ScriptableObjects for shared config/data instead of singletons where possible.
- Never edit `.meta` files or rename assets outside the Editor without warning the user; it breaks references.
